BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UofT St. Michael's College
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261207T193000
DTSTAMP:20261123T155856Z
CREATED:20261123T155642Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261123T155856Z
UID:10007566-1796671800-1796671800@stmikes.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:St. Michael's Schola Cantorum Concert
DESCRIPTION:The St. Michael’s Schola Cantorum\, conducted by Dr. Christina Labriola and joined by Dr. John-Paul Farahat on organ\, presents From the Rising of the Sun to its Setting: music for the Daily Office\, from Matins (Dawn) to Compline (Night). The concert features musical treasures by British liturgical composers past and present: McDowall\, MacMillan\, Howells\, Holst\, Tallis\, Bainton\, Purcell\, Whyte\, and Panufnik. Free admission\, donations welcome. 
URL:https://stmikes.utoronto.ca/event/st-michaels-schola-cantorum-concert
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://stmikes.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Schola-Dec-concert.jpg
END:VEVENT
